  "notes": [
    "Evidence is accumulated across qualified fixes, not a claim that the earlier failed batch commands passed. Native targets are resolved by their last recorded result; the clean release candidate is rerun independently.",
    "The initial native-fixes candidate failure was a stale integer-token/descriptive-name assumption, superseded by candidate.log. Collecting native-loader stress passed unchanged in 288 seconds.",
    "Native-tail owner-image and isolated Host lifecycle image failures under disk pressure were rerun successfully; image-owner-rerun.log and host-8.log are the passing evidence.",
    "The isolated Host entry test needed BIRNAM_TEST_IMAGE; host-image-entry.log supersedes the fixture-less index16 run. Running all ignored Host tests in one VM was invalid and is excluded.",
    "Full installed image CLI passes on prefix25. Prefix26 only retains the prior missing-Module short circuit in addition to the current isLoaded query; its focused Host checks and manifest pass separately.",
    "Core absence includes real projects, TCP/console sessions, LSP and workers with both native providers and authored entry artifacts removed. Optional images declare providers before heap restoration; parent workers remain Store-free.",
    "The native release deadline increases from 900 to 2700 seconds because measured tests exceed the old limit, with no coverage or assertion removed.",
    "GC policy is unchanged. Normal-GC timings are serial, three interleaved fresh-process samples against prefix20; these are composition measurements, not a language-wide speedup.",
    "Older executable images must be rebuilt. Independent Store instances remain explicitly unsupported for persistence. Native artifact/certification self-hosting and generic live mirrors are separate follow-ups."
  ]
